{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>בצרה</b> — This is that He delivered them from under the hand of Egypt. And the meaning of <b>ואענך בסתר רעם</b> — like the way [of]: ענני במרחביה, as though it were written עניתיך, in hiding the thunder from you, at the time HaShem looked down in the pillar of fire and cloud, and it is written: קול רעמך בגלגל." "And the meaning of <b>אבחנך על מי מריבה</b> — the waters of the Rock, for the place was called Massah and Meribah. And the reason to mention this together with that: when you were in water and you crossed the sea, I hid the thunder and the cloud from you, and when you were on dry land, I gave you water." "<b>אבחנך</b> — in the manner of ושם נסהו." "<b>וסלה</b> — in truth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 81, :notes {0 "The comparison to ענני במרחביה (Psalm 118:5) assumes a different vocalization of the same root; left the quoted Hebrew forms untranslated as they represent Ibn Ezra's explicit wordplay."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:44.556913568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}